---
/**
 * About — who "I" is, for the visitor who wants to know before trusting the
 * offer. Linked from the header and footer, never from the argument on /.
 * The portrait holds the left column while the account scrolls beside it: how
 * I work, two jobs as proof of the method, and where the habit of showing the
 * math comes from. Ends on the site's one action.
 */
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Header from '~/components/widgets/Header.astro';
import Button from '~/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import { headerData, mapUrl } from '~/navigation';
import portrait from '~/assets/images/derek-wayne-portrait.jpg';
---

<Layout metadata={{ title: 'About' }}>
  <Fragment slot="header">
    <Header
      links={headerData.links}
      actions={[{ variant: 'primary', text: 'See what to fix first', href: mapUrl }]}
      isSticky
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article
    class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 md:px-6 py-16 md:py-24 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,6fr)] gap-10 lg:gap-20 items-start"
  >
    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt="Derek Wayne standing in a bright white room, smiling, in a dark blazer over a white t-shirt."
      widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200]}
      sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 460px, 100vw"
      class="w-full aspect-4/5 lg:aspect-2/3 rounded-2xl object-cover object-top lg:sticky lg:top-[120px]"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <div class="max-w-152">
      <p class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-label text-secondary">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-heading text-default">
        I'm Derek. I find what slows your business down, and I fix it.
      </h1>
      <a
        href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/derek-wayne/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary"
      >
        <Icon name="tabler:brand-linkedin" class="w-6 h-6" aria-hidden="true" />
        Connect with me on LinkedIn
      </a>

      <p class="mt-8 font-display text-xl leading-relaxed text-default">
        Most owners know something is off. Orders wait, people type the same numbers twice, and month end takes a week.
        You can feel it but can't point to where it starts, and finding that spot is my job.
      </p>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-heading text-default">How I work</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-lg leading-relaxed text-default">
          I look at your business as one system. Work comes in, moves between people and tools, and goes out. I follow
          it until I find the one place where it piles up. Fixing that spot does more than fixing ten others.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-lg leading-relaxed text-default">
          Then I build the fix: a tool your team uses on the work they already do, instead of a report or a slide deck.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-heading text-default">Two jobs, in short</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-lg leading-relaxed text-default">
          ABM needed thousands of maintenance procedures for a chip plant, and each one took a writer half a day. Most
          of that time went to formatting and checking, so I built a tool that does that part. A procedure now takes
          minutes, and the first 400 documents gave back 921 hours of writing time.
          <a
            href="/cases/abm-sop-generator"
            class="whitespace-nowrap font-sans text-base font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary"
            >Read the ABM story</a
          >
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-lg leading-relaxed text-default">
          At Apparel Redefined, one order in ten sat on the dock a week before work could start, because nobody could
          tell which box belonged to which order. Now a receiver scans the box and a screen shows the order it belongs
          to, and only one order in forty waits. Along the way I checked my own $128,000 estimate, found it was wrong,
          and deleted it.
          <a
            href="/cases/apparel-redefined-receiving"
            class="whitespace-nowrap font-sans text-base font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary"
            >Read the Apparel Redefined story</a
          >
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-heading text-default">Why I show the math</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-lg leading-relaxed text-default">
          I came to this work from statistics and data engineering. So every number on this site says how it was
          measured. If I can't show the math, I don't claim the number.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-lg leading-relaxed text-default">
          I have run Rapid Insights for four years, from Toronto. Most of my clients are field service companies and
          manufacturers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="mt-20 border-t border-default/10 pt-12">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-heading text-default">
          Find where your business is losing money.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The Free Process Map takes under 8 minutes and shows what to fix first.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <Button variant="primary" text="See what to fix first" href={mapUrl} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
